    {
      "decision_template": "Series PMOS pull-up stack (W_PU={w_pu}um, L={l_val}um) sized 2x single PMOS",
      "reason": "Series PMOS stack suffers from both hole mobility (~2x lower than electron) AND series resistance stacking penalty. Sizing W=2× compensates the combined effect, achieving symmetric logic threshold. This is why NOR is larger than NAND in CMOS.",
      "tradeoffs": "NOR gate is ~2x the area of a NAND gate with equivalent drive strength. NAND is preferred for area-critical designs.",
      "alternatives": ["Replace deep NOR with NAND + inversion (DeMorgan)", "Pseudo-NMOS NOR (smaller, but static power)"],
